---
alwaysApply: true
---

rules:

-   goal: "Write clean, well-documented, and maintainable code"
-   prefer:
    -   "TypeScript over JavaScript"
    -   "Python with type hints and modern best practices"
    -   "Small, testable functions"
-   avoid:
    -   "Hardcoded values"
    -   "Undocumented changes"
-   style: "Follow ESLint and Prettier conventions"
-   python:
    -   "Always use uv from astral (https://github.com/astral-sh/uv) for Python project management"
    -   "Use uv workspaces when managing multiple related Python projects"
    -   "Always include ruff for linting and formatting Python code"
    -   "Configure ruff in pyproject.toml or ruff.toml with appropriate rules"
    -   "Use uv to manage dependencies, virtual environments, and project setup"
-   edits:
    -   "Always edit only small, focused code sections at a time"
    -   "Make incremental changes rather than large refactorings in a single edit"
    -   "Break down larger changes into multiple smaller, manageable edits"
-   typing:
    -   "Always prefer explicit typing when possible"
    -   "Use TypeScript types, interfaces, and type annotations extensively"
    -   "Avoid 'any' type and prefer specific types or generics"
    -   "Add type annotations to function parameters, return values, and variables when they improve clarity"
-   language:
    -   "All code must be in English: comments, variable names, function names, class names, documentation, error messages, and all other code elements"
    -   "Always respond in English, regardless of the user's language"
    -   "Naming conventions must follow English conventions (camelCase, PascalCase, snake_case, etc.)"
    -   "All constants must always be in UPPERCASE (e.g., MAX_SIZE, API_KEY, DEFAULT_TIMEOUT)"
    -   "All code comments and documentation strings must be written in English"
